# Byte-exact artifacts: git must not touch the line endings of these files.
#
# community/directory.json is verified with crypto.verify() over its literal bytes — by
# scripts/check.js and, at run time, by src/main/community.js. The signature in
# community/directory.sig covers the LF bytes that upstream committed, so any checkout that
# converts them to CRLF (the default on Windows when core.autocrlf=true) makes both checks fail
# with "signature does not verify". The data is not corrupt; the checkout is.
#
# The fix is to pin the bytes, not to re-sign: there is no community.key in this repository and
# re-signing upstream's directory with a new keypair would misrepresent who signed it.
community/directory.json        -text
community/directory.sig         -text
community/community.pub.pem     -text

# Bundled binary and hashed payloads — already detected as binary by git, pinned explicitly so a
# future checkout policy can never rewrite them.
assets/adblock.engine           -text
assets/fonts/*.ttf              -text
